{#-
  Compound V3 — supply / withdraw, base-asset only.

  Every entry in deposit_assets is treated as a Compound V3 BASE asset:
  the template resolves its market via aliases.compound[<asset_lower>_market]
  with NO existence guard. If the alias is missing on the active chain,
  rendering throws (`throwOnUndefined: true`) — there is no silent
  fall-through and no collateral-only path. To grant the Safe access to a
  market, add the asset to deposit_assets AND make sure the matching
  market alias exists in aliases/<chain>/compound.yaml.

  Required template params:
    deposit_assets — list of token alias keys, each of which must be the
                     base asset of a Compound V3 market on the active
                     chain. Example: ["USDC", "USDT", "WETH"].
                     - aliases.tokens[<key>]            must exist
                     - aliases.compound[<key_lower>_market] must exist
                     Either lookup missing ⇒ render-time error naming the
                     undefined key.

  Output shape:
    - One approve role per asset; spender = oneOf(all resolved markets),
      so the Safe can approve any in-scope market to spend any in-scope
      base asset (covers same-market and cross-market approvals — handy
      if Compound later adds collateral support for a base asset).
    - One supply/withdraw role per resolved market; asset = oneOf(all
      deposit_assets). Over-permissioning across (market, asset) pairs is
      harmless: Compound reverts on unsupported pairs at the contract
      layer.

  Not supported by this template:
    - Posting non-base-asset collateral (e.g. WBTC, wstETH, LINK). Those
      assets have no `<asset>_market` alias and listing them throws.
      A future variant can split into base / collateral lists if needed.
-#}
{%- from "_macros/common.tmpl" import approve -%}
{%- set markets = [] -%}
{%- for token in deposit_assets -%}
  {%- set _ = markets.push(aliases.compound[(token | lower) + "_market"]) -%}
{%- endfor -%}
roles:
{%- for token in deposit_assets %}
  {{ approve(aliases.tokens[token], markets) | indent(2) }}
{%- endfor %}
{%- for comet in markets %}

  - address: "{{ comet }}"
    functions:
      - signature: "function supply(address asset, uint256 amount)"
        execution_options: "none"
        params:
          - name: asset
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "oneOf"
            values:
              {%- for token in deposit_assets %}
              - "{{ aliases.tokens[token] }}"
              {%- endfor %}
            value_type: "address"
          - name: amount
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "pass"

      - signature: "function withdraw(address asset, uint256 amount)"
        execution_options: "none"
        params:
          - name: asset
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "oneOf"
            values:
              {%- for token in deposit_assets %}
              - "{{ aliases.tokens[token] }}"
              {%- endfor %}
            value_type: "address"
          - name: amount
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "pass"
{%- endfor %}
